    "title": "The trip page: days, order, times against hours, and the map",
    "why": "decisions/0174 release 3 (accepted 2026-11-19). Each trip gets its own page. Pick the day it starts, how many days and when each day starts; drag stops into order or onto another day (↑ ↓ and a day on a phone), and choose how long at each. Every stop gets a time from the drive before it; with a date, each is checked against its hours ('Closed when you'd arrive: Opens 11 AM', with Move to day 2) and outdoor places against daylight. Times are in the trip's first stop's zone, always labelled; a stop in another zone shows its own. The map numbers the stops, a colour a day, with straight lines between; the miles and times say 'about' (routes come with release 5). Print. The Trip Planner gets Save as a trip, whose page offers the place's ready-made journeys (Use these stops). Add to a trip moves onto the map's card and search's Peek (where the planner's results open), as release 2 moved it here. No AI, no outside calls, no cost.",
